{
  "transactions": [
    { "id": "tx_123", "amount": 1000, "currency": "USD", "created_at": "2026-07-25T12:34:56Z", "description": "Payment" }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "next_cursor": "YmFzZTY0X2luY3JlcHRlZF9zdHJpbmc=", 
    "has_more": true,
    "page_size": 100
  }
}
Cursor format: opaque base64(created_at + "|" + id); server will query with WHERE (created_at, id) < (cursor) and we’ll add a composite index on (user_id, created_at DESC, id) to keep this efficient. Default behavior: no params returns the first page (most recent 100) and the top-level shape remains identical for existing clients; we will not compute total_count. Next steps: implement code, add DB migration for the index, and add unit/integration tests (default, cursor, large-user perf); please confirm page_size=100 or propose a different default.
